    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (71.95) and **Jackson Merrill** (69.89), our premier plays against Kevin Gausman and Huascar Brazob\u00e1n, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% platoon edge and favorable conditions against a pitcher whose slow delivery profile invites a high probability of stolen base attempts\u2014a critical metric for our roster composition. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is a high-conviction start; beyond his strong 13% platoon advantage, he carries an elite BvP history against Brazob\u00e1n (32 PA), which bolsters his floor despite a slight park penalty. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.47) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.40) also serve as high-efficiency pillars, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** specifically seeing his value climb due to a significant 14% platoon advantage against Michael Soroka.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation today involved **Miguel Vargas**, who sits on the bench with a 48.25 score. **Miguel Vargas** was sidelined primarily due to the daunting matchup against Aaron Nola, whose 3.70 xERA combined with an elite catcher framing threat suppressed his projection just enough to keep him behind the efficiency of **Nasim Nunez**. While **Nasim Nunez** faces his own challenges in the #8 spot, the optimizer favored his versatility and the cumulative score benefits of our current outfield alignment. We must keep a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Josh Jung**; while we have modeled them in favorable high-order slots, any downward shift in their actual batting order could force a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores, particularly for **Josh Jung** (59.49), who sits right on the cusp of our \"Strong\" start threshold.",
